[ ] Script the specification release $From 2026-10-13: v0.3.0 was cut by hand (changelog heading for the pending entries, every schema \$id moved, annotated tag on main, release fast-forwarded to publish clearhead.dev), and two commits had no changelog entry until release time. A scripts/release <version> does the mechanical steps and refuses when a commit since the last tag touched spec files without a changelog entry; choosing the version and deciding to publish stay with Darrion. Releasing includes adopting it, in the same session: Core declares the new version (Cargo.toml metadata, schema URLs, CHANGELOG) and the platform pins both, with this checkout on release. v0.3.0 sat unadopted for a day (2026-10-14).$ ^2026-10-13T07:54 #01a13441-b0e0-7ea1-9deb-eadc13a16cf1
[ ] Gate validates examples against the schemas =schema-gate $From review 20261102-024334/10: .sandbox/gate only checks that JSON parses, so examples are checked against schemas by reading. The steward ran jsonschema by hand for v0.4.0 and all nine examples behaved as named. Make the gate run a real validator, valid_* and invalid_* by name, available in the sandbox. Also add the .sandbox/prompt.md this repo lacks, so reviews get its project rules.$ !3 ^2026-11-02T03:01 #01a19a34-d347-7b62-baea-f5cc8fbc4bd3
[ ] Specify the archive and unarchive action results =spec-move-result $From review 20261102-030308/8 of =ci-core. transaction_result.schema.json defines no result for archive action or unarchive action, since transact has no archive operation, so Core v-next prints the transaction envelope with operation kinds archived and unarchived outside the schema's enum. Steward's how-level call for that release, pending this. What the specification says is Darrion's: raise it as a Decision with the next specification release, not before.$ +steward ^2026-11-02T04:26 #01a19a82-8edf-7701-a2f8-9db682789866
[ ] Make Habit plannedFrom coherent across prose, shape and fixture =spec-habit-planned-from $Found reviewing run habit-graph-20261104 (core-habit-graph). ontology.md:147 says a Habit derives app:plannedFrom 'as for an action's block', but shape:PlannedBlock targets only app:Action, so examples/conformance/habits/app.ttl validates with plannedStart and no plannedFrom. Core 18e8f91 follows the prose and emits it; its exact-triples test filters the derived triple to match the fixture. Draft: add plannedFrom to the Habit fixture and extend PlannedBlock to app:Habit (or state that Habits don't derive it). Either way it changes what the spec says: open with ⏸ Decision to Darrion, then drop the filter in habit_graph_conformance.rs once the release is pinned.$ !4 ^2026-11-04T07:47 #01a1a586-c835-7440-8499-2136361b77bf
